/*
time complexity - O(logn) -> array gets divided into two parts at each step 
space complexity - O(1)
INTUITION
1. Binary search repeatedly cuts the array in half.

You are searching in a sorted array, so every comparison lets you eliminate half the search space.

2. Compute mid and compare with the target.

At each step:

If nums[mid] == target → answer found.

If nums[mid] < target → target can only be in the right half.

If nums[mid] > target → target can only be in the left half.

3. Shrink the search boundaries.

Move either:

l = mid + 1 (search in the right side), or

r = mid - 1 (search in the left side)

Each move discards half the array.

4. If pointers cross, target doesn’t exist.

When l > r, all possibilities are exhausted → return -1.
*/

class Solution {
    public int search(int[] nums, int target) {
        int n = nums.length;
        int l =0;
        int r = n-1;
        while(l<=r){
            int mid = (l+r)/2;
            if(nums[mid]==target)return mid;
            else if(target>nums[mid]){
                l=mid+1;
            }
            else{
                r=mid-1;
            }
        }
        return -1;

    }
}
